# Example environment variables for local development
# Copy this file to .dev.vars and fill in your actual API keys
# Never commit .dev.vars to git!

# Finnhub API (Real-time stock quotes)
# Get your free API key at: https://finnhub.io/register
FINNHUB_API_KEY=your_finnhub_api_key_here

# Twelve Data API (Historical candles for stock charts)
# Get your free API key at: https://twelvedata.com/
# Free tier: 8 API calls/minute, 800 calls/day
TWELVE_DATA_API_KEY=your_twelve_data_api_key_here

# CoinGecko API (Crypto OHLC and price data)
# Get your free API key at: https://www.coingecko.com/en/api/pricing
COINGECKO_API_KEY=your_coingecko_api_key_here

# Marketaux API (Financial news)
# Get your key at: https://www.marketaux.com/
MARKETAUX_API_TOKEN=your_marketaux_token_here

# Gold API
# Get your key at: https://www.goldapi.io/
GOLD_API_KEY=your_gold_api_key_here

# Workers AI is provided via the native `[ai] binding = "AI"` in wrangler.toml.
# No GEMINI_API_KEY (or other LLM API token) is required for analysis.
# Optional overrides (also settable in wrangler.toml [vars]; validated in src/core/aiConfig.ts):
# AI_MODEL=@cf/zai-org/glm-4.7-flash
# AI_MAX_COMPLETION_TOKENS=2048
# AI_TEMPERATURE=0.7
#
# Local AI: `wrangler dev` uses your Cloudflare account for the AI binding when authenticated.
# Mocked unit tests do not require live inference (see `npm test` in worker/).
